DHM Design | 4
3. Project Area
Familiarity with the Capitol Basin and the West Edge District
The DHM Design team is very familiar with the project area. Having been involved
with the West Edge EPA assessment grant and Area Wide Planning eff orts, DHM
Design brings intimate knowledge of the role Civic Center Commons as in important
community amenity along with the stormwater function. Additionally DHM Design
has worked on several other recent projects in Cheyenne including Converse and
Cahill Parks. Meetings for these projects have included coordinating with multiple
City departments, the MPO, the DDA, County representatives, land owners and the
public to understand current issues, challenges, and opportunities.
Our team deliberately brings additional local presence with a many of our team
members. Benchmark Engineering is very familiar with the project area. Thier offi  ce is
located extremely close to the project site, catty-corner to the site.  Additionally, BME
has an extensive knowledge of the stormwater drainage system, including proposed
improvements, throughout the Capitol Basin.  In recent years, BME completed the
civil engineering plans for various facilities in the basin:
• Capitol Basin 26th Interceptor Storm Sewer (currently in design phase)
• Cheyenne Regional Medical Center
• Emergency Department
• Cancer Center
• Parking Garage
• Numerous utility upgrades, relocations and improvements
• Wyoming State Capital Square Rehabilitation and Restoration
• Herschler Building
• Capitol Building
• New Central Utility Plant
• Pioneer Avenue Parking Lot
• St. Mary’s Parking Lot
• Public Safety Center
• Laramie County Library
• St. Mary’s School
• Capitol Basin Brownfi eld Redevelopment Peer Review
• Cheyenne DDA Curb and Gutter Replacement, Phase I
• Snyder Avenue Reconnaissance and Peer Review
• Dinneen Building Renovations
• Meridian Trust Federal Credit Union
```

