11 | West Edge District Civic Center Commons
5. References
Cheyenne West Edge Redevelopment
Economic development blossoms when arts and cultural investments
bring people into the community. For the City of Cheyenne’s West Edge
neighborhood, DHM Design’s goal is to strategically shape the physical and
social character of the area around arts and cultural activities following
assessment and remediation of the brownfi eld properties. DHM Design
is currently leading a team of consultants funded with an EPA brownfi eld
planning grant to provide help the community redevelop the a revitalized
downtown. This eff ort follows on related work by DHM Design as part of
a larger brownfi eld planning team to create a vision for vibrant infi ll of
historic and warehouse blocks applying improved streetscape, a system of new public parks,
and adaptive reuse of currently vacant landmark buildings. Instead of traveling elsewhere for
entertainment and cultural experiences, residents will invest in the local economy. This newly
created centralized park and connected parkway system will preserve the historic character of
the near west side while creating new vibrant public venues. The project gained enthusiastic
support using concerts, video, 3D modeling and social media.
www.cheyennewestedge.com
