8. Project Speciﬁ c InformaƟ on
The West Edge Vision
Civic commons holds the potential to play a pivotal role in the revitalization of the
West Edge. The addition of an attractive public green with a perimeter of pedestrian
oriented streetscape is something that investors and land owners have shown great
support and anticipation. It is a commitment of public funding and services that will
aff ect land values and create a larger draw for people to visit downtown.
West Edge is already host to small enterprise type businesses looking for aff ordable
locations that also off er the benefi ts of being downtown. The input from the stakeholders
and the public for the EPA planning initiative underscores the demand and growth
potential for leasing to high tech, start –up, and creative type businesses who value
the historic building stock, and seek like-minded entrepreneurs. Additionally, an
opportunity to greatly expand both rental and for sale housing in the West Edge area
emerged in the EPA planning project research and public input process. With interest in
more housing and a range of infi ll development, we have heard repeated requests for
continued City investment in improved streetscape, walking routes and public green
space. The West Edge vision plans completed prior to this project provided a glimpse
of program elements suggested by the City and public, and make suggestions for
potential materials and theming possibilities.
Embracing the train and warehouse culture, the West Edge promotes a brand associated
with a gritty fl avor of brick and metal. This style encourages the coexistence of old
and new to achieve a homegrown character that doesn’t just mimic other regional
communities, but off ers a more narrowly targeted sense of place. Building on the
mix of historic and contemporary forms, fostering creativity, building involvement
of the local stakeholders, and encouraging synergistic land use is key to continuing
momentum in the West Edge movement.
Achieving a Vibrant Stormwater Park
Civic parks are a crucial component of thriving downtowns. The West Edge vision
aims to achieve a vibrant, attractive park in the core of downtown Cheyenne while
simultaneously handling storm water functions as part of the larger regional system.
The early concepts for the park grew from vision of a central outdoor green space
that many layered functions that would in turn increase property values and boost
the desirability of this location for investment.
```

