Master Plan and Design Development
After incorporating review comments and the approval of refi ned master plan, the
design team generally provides design development plans that include layout of
facilities, grading of drainage plans, utilities, materials, landscaping, irrigation and site
details. Plans are prepared in AutoCAD format and are the basis for accurate opinions
of cost. DHM Design would have a geotechnical report prepared as part of the design
development process, adding validity to design decisions.  Plan sets will be provided
at the 50% completion for review.
During the Design Development process, DHM Design would also provide to the City,
a preliminary set of specifi cations for City staff  review.
Opinions Of Cost
DHM Design understands the importance of accurate cost estimating. We believe
that very detailed estimates, all inclusive of permits, fees, utility services, construction,
testing, design, administration and infl ation lead to more accurate park development
costs. DHM Design works closely with local consultants and contractors to prepare
detailed estimates for construction at numerous stages of the design process.
Final Construction Documents
With approval from City Staff  of the Design Development package, DHM Design would
prepare fi nal Construction Documents and specifi cations for site improvements. As part
of the Construction Documents package, DHM Design also includes fi nal specifi cations
for construction as well as a fi nal Opinion of Cost for the project.
Experience with Bidding and Construction Management
Our team has extensive experience assisting our clients with bidding and construction
services. DHM Design regularly helps client’s package fi nal documents for advertising
and distribution to contractors. We prepare agendas and attend pre-bid conferences
to address questions and prepare follow up addenda for distribution to bidders.
We also have extensive construction observation experience and will assist the City
through the entire process.  Our staff  is knowledgeable regarding installation methods,
required testing procedures and quality control that is important to the fi nal built
product. This construction knowledge also helps us in the preparation of construction
details, plans and specifi cations. Our Principals & Project Manger’s are integrally involved
in daily construction management of all of our projects.
We also assist our clients perform the following tasks as needed:
• Weekly project meetings (with contractor and City staff ) and distribution of meeting
minutes.
• The design team will provide shop drawing and submittal review as necessary per
the specs.
• Respond to Requests for Information (RFI)
• Issue Supplemental Instructions
• Review Change Orders
• Review and certify contractor’s application for payment
• Review material test reports
• Record changes to the contract documents
• Provide daily construction observation with fi eld reports at regular intervals or at
critical points in construction.
• Provide substantial and fi nal completion services
• Assistance with Warranty inspection
• Record drawings coordination with contractor and submittal
Our team has extensive experience overseeing and coordinating multiple projects
concurrently. Each week, we may work on as many as 4 to 6 diff erent projects. This is
our normal business model, where projects are all in diff erent stages of the design and
construction process. We prepare a detailed schedule for each project to track required
time and allocate staff  resources. Our Parks Team staff  (Principals, Project Managers
and production staff ) work very closely on all aspects of each project, meeting several
